nd safety injection devices, as well as digital applications to assist people with managing patient's diabetes. It primarily sells its products to wholesalers and distributors. The company was formerly known as Berra Newco, Inc. Embecta Corp. was founded in 1924 and is headquartered in Parsippany, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Devdatt  Kurdikar Ph.D. | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $470K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $79K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Embecta Corp. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $446M market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 34% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 26-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 66% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $182M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.01\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.7pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 86/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 22% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 92% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 65% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Embecta (EMBC) Q4 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/embecta-embc-q4-2026-earnings-191822000.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795548332.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.15,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Embecta Corp (EMBC) (Q4 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Strong Q4 Growth and Owen Mumford Boost ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/embecta-corp-embc-q4-2026-162059435.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795537259.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.927,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Results: Embecta Corp. Beat Earnings Expectations And Analysts Now Have New Forecasts","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-embc/embecta/news/results-embecta-corp-beat-earnings-expectations-and-analysts","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795782066.855,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.556,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Embecta to Participate in BofA Securities 2026 Leveraged Finance Conference","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/embecta-participate-bofa-securities-2026-220000062.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795644000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Embecta Q4 Earnings Call Highlights","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.y